bitcurator-mounter (0.4.4~beta1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix build on Ubuntu 22.04, whose setuptools 59.6 cannot parse the
    pyproject.toml [project] table (PEP 621 requires setuptools >= 61) and
    produced an UNKNOWN-0.0.0 wheel. debian/rules now upgrades setuptools in
    the build environment via pip, guarded to run only when the installed
    setuptools is too old, so 24.04 and 26.04 (which already satisfy the
    requirement and enforce PEP 668) are unaffected.
  * debian/control: add python3-pip and ca-certificates to Build-Depends for
    the setuptools upgrade. Note that the 22.04 build now requires network
    access and no longer builds offline in a clean chroot.

 -- BitCurator Consortium <bitcurator@gmail.com>  Thu, 11 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bitcurator-mounter (0.4.3~beta1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * policyapp.py: prevent re-entrant policy dialogs. Activating a menu item
    while its confirmation dialog was already open spawned a second dialog;
    a guard now blocks further activations until the open dialog is dismissed,
    and both toggle items are greyed while a dialog is in progress.
  * Correct placeholder tray-icon colours: read-only is now green (safe) and
    writeable is red (danger), matching the risk the state represents.

 -- BitCurator Consortium <bitcurator@gmail.com>  Wed, 10 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bitcurator-mounter (0.4.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * udisks.py: fix device enumeration crash on startup. GLib.Variant property
    values from GetManagedObjects were unwrapped with a nonexistent
    get_python_value() method; use the correct GLib.Variant.unpack() instead.
    Affected every bc-mounter launch (AttributeError before the window opened).

 -- BitCurator Consortium <bitcurator@gmail.com>  Wed, 10 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bitcurator-mounter (0.4.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * debian/control: depend on "polkitd | policykit-1" and "pkexec |
    policykit-1" instead of the policykit-1 transitional package, which has
    been removed on Ubuntu 26.04. The alternatives keep 22.04 (where both
    come from policykit-1) building while satisfying 24.04 and 26.04 with the
    split polkitd and pkexec packages.

 -- BitCurator Consortium <bitcurator@gmail.com>  Wed, 10 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bitcurator-mounter (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rewrite of the legacy bc_mounter.py and bc_policyapp.py scripts.
  * Replace rbfstab fstab-rewriting with a udev/udisks2/polkit mechanism:
    - block-layer write protection via blockdev --setro
    - automount suppression (UDISKS_AUTO=0) to avoid the hotplug race
    - journal-safe read-only mount options via udisks2 mount_options.conf
    - BITCURATOR-SAVE label exemption for writeable persistent storage
  * GTK3 + AyatanaAppIndicator3 + dasbus; supports Ubuntu 22.04/24.04/26.04
    from a single codebase.
  * New privileged helper bc-mountpolicy (invoked via pkexec) replaces
    direct rbfstab invocation.

 -- BitCurator Consortium <bitcurator@gmail.com>  Wed, 10 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
